<title>USA: Continental dismisses Delta complaint.</title>
<headline>Continental dismisses Delta complaint.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines Inc said on Thursday that Delta Air Lines Inc's petition to revoke Continental's route between New York/Newark to Rio de Janeiro and Sao Paulo is &quot;ridiculous.&quot;</p>
<p>Continental said in a statement that its Newark-Sao Paulo/Rio de Janeiro service complies with the conditions imposed by the Department of Transportation.</p>
<p>Delta said on July 2 that it would file a petition with the U.S. Department of Transportation to revoke an award of Brazil frequencies to Continental so Delta could begin its own service.</p>
<p>Delta said that Continental has abandoned its proposed two aircraft service.</p>
</text>
